PATCH 215: reconstruct FUN_0000_7b91 (the DCBS TANK-object per-type INIT method dispatched by c296's
tail near-vector) -- the next DGROUP-near-offset base-loss in the DCBS object-init family.  Asm-verified
vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin 0x7b91-0x7bce.

Reached only after patch 214 makes c296's per-type dispatch fire with di (the object near-offset) live.
7b91 was pristine Ghidra: `*(param_1 + 0xad) = 0xf` etc. with param_1 = di (0xc05c) treated as a HOST
pointer -> SIGSEGV.  DS=DGROUP=0x1c00; every `[di+N]` is a DS-relative byte/word field (the asm uses
movw/movb at 0xad/0xaf/0xb1/0xb3/0x8d/0xb5/0x87/0x14/0x16).  The tail copies a seg-0x2c7f template into
the object body at DGROUP:di+0xbf via 1e27 (patch 087: 1e27 takes a NEAR-OFFSET dst and bases it
internally, so di+0xbf is passed as the near offset).  Reconstructed with the explicit DGROUP base +
the asm byte/word widths.

Validated by the crash advancing: DCBS record 0 (enemy slot 0xc05c) now installs FULLY (c296 + 7b91
both return), and record 1 (0xc157 = 0xc05c+0xfb, the enemy stride) advances to a DIFFERENT per-type
init method (FUN_0000_8744 -- the next same-class base-loss = the new frontier).

Cascade-only => BEHAVIOUR-NEUTRAL for the 19 verify flows (same reachability as 214: DCBS parse only).
Sources pristine; fist.c via build/.
